# Copy to `.env` for local development:  cp .env.example .env
#
# ⛔ WHERE THE BAKED SLAB COMES FROM. Since 2026-09-01 `public/baked/` is NOT in git
# (516 MiB, growing 100–400 MB per town, against a 1 GB GitHub Pages limit). It is
# served from R2. A fresh clone therefore has NO ground, buildings, trees or terrain
# on disk, and without this line the app asks the dev server for them and gets 404s —
# a map with nothing on it.
#
# ⭐ Leave it UNSET if you are authoring: unset means ASSET_BASE falls back to
# BASE_URL, i.e. whatever you have baked locally under public/baked/, which is what
# you want when you are re-pouring a scene and need to see your own output.
#
# ⛔ There is deliberately NO automatic fallback to R2 when a local file is missing.
# That would make a broken local bake look like a working one — the failure class this
# whole arc exists to close. Missing means missing, loudly.
VITE_ASSET_BASE=https://assets.theward.online/

# Apps Script deployment URL — see PUBLISH.md §"Single source of truth".
# VITE_API_URL=

# Supabase (Cary). Absent is fine — the stub client keeps the app functional.
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
